# BEACON Token Service - Laptop Version (POC)
# Copy this file to .env and fill in your Azure credentials
# NEVER commit the actual .env file to git!

# ============================================
# AZURE AD CONFIGURATION
# ============================================
# Get these from Azure Portal > App Registrations > Your App
TENANT_ID=your-azure-tenant-id-here
CLIENT_ID=your-app-client-id-here
CLIENT_SECRET=your-client-secret-here

# ============================================
# SERVER CONFIGURATION
# ============================================
PORT=3000
NODE_ENV=development

# ============================================
# SETUP INSTRUCTIONS
# ============================================
# 1. Copy this file:
#    cp .env.example .env
#
# 2. Go to Azure Portal (portal.azure.com)
#
# 3. Navigate to: Azure Active Directory > App registrations
#
# 4. Create new app or select existing:
#    - Name: "BEACON Token Service"
#    - Supported account types: "Single tenant"
#    - No redirect URI needed
#
# 5. Copy these values to .env above:
#    - TENANT_ID: Overview > Directory (tenant) ID
#    - CLIENT_ID: Overview > Application (client) ID
#
# 6. Create client secret:
#    - Go to: Certificates & secrets > New client secret
#    - Description: "BEACON POC" (or your preference)
#    - Expires: 12 months (set calendar reminder!)
#    - Copy the VALUE (not ID) to CLIENT_SECRET above
#    - WARNING: Value only shown once - save it immediately!
#
# 7. Power BI API permissions (may be auto-included):
#    - Go to: API permissions > Add permission
#    - Select: Power BI Service
#    - Delegated: Report.Read.All, Dataset.Read.All
#    - Click: Grant admin consent
#
# 8. Configure Power BI workspace:
#    - Go to Power BI Service (app.powerbi.com)
#    - Open workspace settings
#    - Go to: Access > Add people or groups
#    - Add your service principal as "Member"
#    - Format: app:[CLIENT_ID]@[TENANT_ID]
#
# 9. Enable service principal tenant setting:
#    - Go to: Power BI Admin portal > Tenant settings
#    - Enable: "Allow service principals to use Power BI APIs"
#    - Apply to: Entire organization (or specific security group)
#
# ============================================
# SECURITY NOTES (POC ACCEPTABLE)
# ============================================
# ✓ HTTP OK for laptop version (local network only)
# ✓ .env file OK (never commit to git)
# ✓ CORS * OK (development only)
# ✓ Password SSH OK (for initial setup)
#
# ⚠ CLIENT_SECRET expires every 12 months
#   - Set calendar reminder 2 weeks before expiration
#   - Create new secret, update .env, restart service
#
# ⚠ For production deployment:
#   - Use cloud-version with HTTPS
#   - Store secrets in Azure Key Vault
#   - Restrict CORS to specific origins
#   - Use key-based SSH only
#   - See: ../cloud-version/.env.example
#
# ============================================
# TESTING
# ============================================
# After setup, test with:
#   npm install
#   npm start
#   curl http://localhost:3000/health
#
# Expected response:
#   {"status":"healthy","timestamp":"...","uptime":...}
